gs TBD; numbers need a conversion rule or bigint acceptance).\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:158:(§8.1), as a foreign engine's layout is, and does not enter A.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:223:where `L(p)` is the standard live-in set at the resume pc `p` (§8.1),\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:557:   liveness of §8.1 is computed over the real successor relation, in\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:724:`saved(pc, rd)` from A (§8.1) and refuses a window with a register\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:778:from A (§8.1), and keeps `:yin.safepoint/layout` as a map from physical\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:838:checksum are regenerated then, mechanically (derivations design §8.1-8.2).\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:863:### 8.1 Static facts per pc: def, use, live\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:928:     windows are `saved(p, rd)` at *reachable* safepoints (§8.1), and\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:949:     operands (step 3) and every saved window come from §8.1's\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:965:   virtual live-out over the instruction's **actual successors** (§8.1)\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1024:at the slice and once at cutover (derivations design §8.1); nothing is\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1061:descriptors lose their lift declaration (derivations design §8.1-8.2);\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1084:   loader rules of §3.4 (both load paths), **and the §8.1 analysis\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files collab | rg '1794600000000|attribution|addendum'; cat docs/agents/routing-status.md; cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files collab | rg '1794600000000|attribution|addendum'; cat docs/agents/routing-status.md; cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.glm-5.3.stdout.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794610000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.qwen-review.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.astra-review.stdout.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a.astra-review.stdout.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794620000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.kimi-review.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-DRAFT.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.prompt.md\\ncollab/orch-lane/1794600000000-engineer-roundA-p1-fixes.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.stdout.log\\ncollab/yang-python/1793410000000-orchestrator-yang-python-attribution-note.md\\ncollab/dao-jing/1790012238375-architect-jing-cbor-eve-addendum.prompt.md\\ncollab/yin-vm/1790016536012-architect-debruijn-vm-revision-r4-addendum.prompt.md\\ncollab/yin-vm/1791990000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase5c-r2.mutant-addendum.md\\n# Delegate routing status\\n\\nDurable record of owner-relayed delegate CLI/model availability and budget\\nstatus. No tool exposes this automatically (weekly quotas, provider outages,\\nspending caps) — the owner relays it in conversation, and it otherwise dies\\nwith that session. This file is what lets a different orchestrator seat, in a\\nfresh session with no shared history, know the current routing constraints\\nwithout re-asking or discovering them the hard way.\\n\\nAppend-only in spirit, like `docs/orchestrator-log.md`: when a status goes\\nstale or is superseded, add a new entry rather than editing the old one, so\\nthe history of what was true when stays visible. Unlike the work log, this\\nfile may be edited to trim entries that are long superseded and no longer\\nuseful context, since this is a status board, not a provenance record.\\n\\nEvery entry states: the destination, what the owner said, when, and how to\\napply it. Treat every entry here as a claim to re-verify (a quota resets, an\\noutage resolves), not as permanent authority — the same posture as the work\\nlog.\\n\\n## How to apply\\n\\nBefore routing a new dispatch to any metered/quota-based destination, check\\nthis file's most recent entry for that destination. If none exists or the\\nstated reset time has passed, the status is unknown — proceed normally, but\\nconsider a cheap sanity check (a trivial prompt) before committing a\\nreal task to a destination that failed recently. When the owner relays a new\\nstatus in conversation, add an entry here before continuing, so it survives\\npast the current session.\\n\\n## Current status\\n\\n2026-11-04 measured — qwen-code LIVE: Alibaba's `qwen` CLI configured on the Token Plan and verified\\nDistinct from the withdrawn claude-wrapper of this morning: `qwen` now means `@qwen-code/qwen-code@0.17.0` (nvm node v26.1.0 npm-global; a second mise install was found and removed today at the owner's request). The owner's key `sk-sp-H.LXYLM.f0Vo.…` is registered in ~/.qwen/settings.json env; the gateway is https://token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1 (region-bound: the key 403s at cn-beijing). Measured usable catalog: qwen3.8-max / qwen3.8-flash / qwen3.7-max / qwen3.6-flash / deepseek-v4-pro — everything else the pre-existing auto-written config listed is \\\"Access to model denied\\\" or \\\"Model not exist\\\". Headless probe `qwen -p \\\"...\\\" < /dev/null` returned OK rc=0. Session-ID mechanics not yet measured; do not invent them. Consequence: qwen is an available implementation destination NOW; parallel capacity qwen | kimi | glm | muse | codex. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (qwen3.8-flash).\\n\\n2026-11-04 measured then withdrawn — the `qwen` wrapper lane is REMOVED (name collision with Alibaba's `qwen-code` agent)\\nThe Model Studio Token Plan measurement stands (registered via `bl auth login --config token-plan`; Token Plan Anthropic endpoint https://token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/apps/anthropic works end-to-end through a claude-family wrapper; measured catalog qwen3.8-max + qwen3.8-flash only; cn-beijing gateway 403s this key; `bl config agent --agent claude-code` is a global takeover — CAUTION stands). But the `~/.local/bin/qwen` wrapper was deleted the same day: \\\"qwen\\\" collides with Alibaba's separate `qwen-code` coding agent, making the name ambiguous as a delegate. NO qwen dispatch lane is installed; re-create one under a non-colliding name before routing anything here. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-04 owner request — measured: muse-spark-1.3 WORKS on the API-key lane (contributor mode on)\\nProbe on the laptop: `muse exec --trust-workspace --approval-mode never --model muse-spark-1.3` returned OK rc=0 in a fresh trusted dir. `muse usage` reports \\\"No subscription allowance (api_key)\\\" — the run is billed through the persisted API key (~/.config/muse/api-key, keychain auth), not the subscription window. Contributor mode is globally enabled in settings.json. Owner follow-up measured: the explicit ID `--model muse-spark-1.3-contributor` ALSO works (OK rc=0, same recipe) — so both the plain alias with contributor mode inherited from settings and the explicit `-contributor` suffix are valid dispatch forms; the earlier note that \\\"contributor is only the mode, not part of the model ID\\\" was wrong. Consequence: spark-1.3 API dispatches are live regardless of the subscription window state; wonder-1.0 remains the subscription-lane model. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-03 owner relay — codex is available again\\nOwner relay: codex may be dispatched; the 06:10 relay's \\\"no new codex dispatches\\\" line is lifted. Route codex rounds per team.md and delegate-invocation-reference.md as usual. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-03 07:5x +07 — measured: muse headless root-caused on shiva; the recipe works on BOTH servers now\\nThe two shiva failure modes are now reproduced and fixed (entered in delegate-invocation-reference.md): (1) headless `muse exec` without `--trust-workspace` runs UNTRUSTED in any root not in ~/.config/muse/trust.json (only /home/sto/workspace/datomworld is listed server-side) — agent delegation silently off; a trivial probe still passes, so probe-only checks masked it; (2) the default --approval-mode on-request blocks forever headless with no API traffic — measured: a tool-using round hung to SIGTERM at 180s having done zero work. With `--trust-workspace --approval-mode never` a tool-using round completes in seconds; the sandbox (bwrap + user namespaces, both present on shiva AND jupiter) stays ON and the Bubblewrap banner is informational. Verified end-to-end on shiva and jupiter (muse 1.4.14, muse-wonder-1.0): headless muse work rounds are live on both servers. The 04:0x \\\"muse wedges silently on shiva\\\" entry is explained by mechanism (2), not an API outage. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-03 06:10 +07 — owner relay: muse, agy, glm, kimi are the only cli tools available\\n2026-11-03 03:10 +07 — measured: muse subscription window LIVE again (the 06:10 relay's muse lane is open)\\nProbe: `muse exec --model muse-wonder-1.0` with a fresh caller UUID returned \\\"OK\\\" (rc=0) at 03:10 +07 — earlier than the 20:41 window estimate recorded on 11-02; the reset must have been the daily window, not the 24h one. Consequence: muse is the default implementation destination NOW (with the standing kimi code-quality gate); agy stays out until its quota reset (~7 days from the 11-02 exhaustion). No new codex or mistral dispatches (the 06:10 relay). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-03 03:2x +0700 — correction: agy is LIVE on both hosts (the earlier \\\"quota\\\" read was a per-session limit, not account exhaustion)\\nOwner challenged the agy-quota assumption. Measured: fresh `agy --model gemini-4-argon-high` probes return OK on the laptop and on shiva (rc=0, real responses). The 11-02 cljd round died with \\\"Individual quota reached, resets in 165h\\\" — that was the SESSION/turn budget of one 6,600-second 645k-token turn, not the account. Lesson (same class as the muse reset misread): a delegate CLI's own reset estimate is not availability; always probe with a fresh cheap session before ruling a destination out. agy is a live implementation destination NOW (with the standing kimi quality gate); the long-round budget stays a real constraint — split big rounds into resumed sessions rather than one turn. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-03 03:4x +0700 — amendment to the 03:2x correction: agy IS quota-limited after all (intermittent)\\nThe fresh-session probes passed at 03:1x-03:2x, but the dispatched real work round (xlang slice 1 on shiva) died instantly with \\\"Individual quota reached, resets in ~161h\\\", and an immediate laptop probe also returns quota-reached. True shape: the account pool is at its individual ceiling; small probes occasionally squeak through but a real work round cannot complete. AGY: unusable for work rounds until the reset (~161h); the probes' success was the tail of the pool, not availability. Implementation falls back to muse (live) for work rounds; kimi gate unchanged. The seat reverts the 03:2x \\\"live on both hosts\\\" conclusion to: live-for-probes, quota-walled-for-work. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\n2026-11-03 0x:xx +0700 — agy model-level routing (argon walled; claude/flash live); muse-on-shiva WORKS headless with --trust-workspace\\nOwner: \\\"argon has reached quota but gemini-3.8-flash is available and so are agy's claude models.\\\" Measured: claude-opus-5-5-high and gemini-3.8-flash-high probes return