e re-verify.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:349:## 2026-10-29 23:52:11 +07 — NEW TRACK ADOPTED per owner brief: section 8.10 common-call adoption for yang.clojure\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:353:Tree: master@c203c6e6 verified to contain the spec commit eb8030e8 (yang.antlr.md §8.10); NEW worktree yang-common-call (branch yang-common-call, off c203c6e6)\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:354:Done: Owner delivered an orchestrator brief (collab/1793292027721-orchestrator-clojure-common-call.prompt.md): adopt the approved shared calling convention (§8.10, Kimi-approved r1/r2) in yang.clojure as an explicit opt-in, in a three-owner division — TS/PHP orchestrator coordinates the shared runtime; the authoring chat owns Python; this seat owns Clojure adoption. Executed the \\\\\\\"first return\\\\\\\": (1) verified the spec commit is an ancestor of master and read §8.10 in full; (2) PUBLISHED the ownership map (collab/1793297800000-orchestrator-clojure-ownership-map.md): reserved files (yang/clojure.cljc + this track's tests + latte_oracle), consumed-from-coordinating-owner artifacts (the pinned shared runtime module + profile address + A/B vectors), base/worktree (yang-common-call @ c203c6e6), and the rule that slice-9's BLOCKED gate stays preserved on yang-slice9 and is not reclassified; (3) dispatched the Clojure-specific architect rulings to kimi (r3, collab/-architect-yang-call-kimi-r3-clojure.prompt.md): A1 entry publication (descriptor-at-boundary vs constructor-constructed), A2 call-site routing + fast-path obligations, A3 :yang.call/named for a no-named-args dialect, A4 the outcome-model <-> raise-exit two-regime mapping, A5 internal helpers NOT rewritten as descriptors. Flagged to the routing board mentally: kimi is doing architect work per the widened bench; codex engineering chat is the designated implementation lane for bounded assignment