trative example, and it conflicts with 8.10.11's remains-data requirement as realized in open Clojure maps; escalated to the section's approving architect rather than resolved by the seat that created the contradiction.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:1:# Session log — yang.clojure track (hardening + adoption of §8.10 common call)\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:35:Done: glm r3 confirmation (session 3e4d9593, resumed after a plan-only stop): N1 CLOSED (all forged shapes refuse with the qualified :yang.call/not-callable via both operators incl. the def-alias route; admitted + dynamic-eligibility intact both lanes), N2 CLOSED (dao.host.gate-test 14/178; manifests 156/154/155, union 168) — \\\\\\\"Ready for Architect sign-off\\\\\\\". astra sign-off r1 DENIED on a real P2 the seat had not caught: the invocation admission gate skipped ARGUMENT evaluation on refusal (§8.10.4 requires operands once, left-to-right, before the callee check) — reproduced on both lanes at 12feb7d1 vs abbfb998. Fix round to kimi -> committed 45269e0f (all operands bound before the witness check, both branches reuse the bindings, refused/admitted regressions both lanes). This seat verified 143/1484 across the five suites + oracle 21/971 + kondo 0 errors. astra SIGN-OFF GRANTED for 63674368..45269e0f, conditions: final-commit shiva Node/Dart lanes + the dao.stream merge gate.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:46:Done: (1) Re-derived the 33-failure regression on the clean rebased tree: bracket GREEN at the rebase base 0dc5d7af (118/0, adoption included), RED from 211dded9 onward — the gate-closure round was authored on the PRE-adoption base and its self-reported green predates the merge. (2) Root cause, measured by probes on both trees: the round introduced a parallel invoker convention — `fn?` stripped of its `yang.call/eligible?` fallback (so `(fn? first)`=false for §8.