dening-3-design.gpt-6-astra.*): seven slices — H3-0 restore declared dispositions + trustworthy evidence (lands first, harness-only); H3-1 diagnose the two blocked fixtures (finding: all three blocked C executions hit \\\\\\\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\\\\\\\" at 2,000,000 steps; authorized 2M/4M/8M diagnostic trials, NOT an automatic budget raise); H3-2 proof elaboration (11 arities) via end-to-end proof fixtures starting from the repaired check-assume-have-discharge; H3-3a/b syntax (17) + env/unparser/utils (11); H3-4 presyntax+typing (9; parse/1 direct fixture, poisoned-parse/1 regression preserved); H3-5 normalization (10); H3-6 final audit — independent credit reconstruction from raw traces, 165/165, the (:gate-status) assertion unchanged. Guardrails: executed-arity rule frozen, four departures + two upstream failures stay declared, admission denominator (165/10, 146/9) closed to incidental change, no yang.call/yin.vm changes without a ruling, intermediate sign-offs are not kernel closure, credit withdrawal must always be explained. Two architect findings sharpened the scope: the blocked fixtures' immediate failure is the 2M-step budget (legitimate cost vs repeated work/continuation defects undistinguished), and the deviation classifier is representation-stale (expects a bare closure at :meta; refreshed outcomes carry a §8.10 callable descriptor). (2) H3-0 routed to codex engineering per the plan (worktree h30, brief collab/1793790000000-engineer-h3-0-declared-dispositions.prompt.md): declarations as versioned input, representation-aware classification validated against actual runtime representation (a {:type :closure} map is insufficient), negative controls (mutated call / unrelated id / changed payload / forged representation / incomplete lane), writer round-trip tests, the stale narrative refresh (145/165 and \\\\\\\"only 20\\\\\\\" are dead — 107/58 is the truth), and the expected end state 100/2/2/2 with 107 credited 58 remaining and the gate still