he owner-ruled cell/authentic? policy (yin.vm additive + the shared _descriptor + the yang.clojure sites); the yang.clojure↔TS matrix skip is CLOSED (matrix 13/21/0 on jupiter). This seat: the TS/PHP authenticity sweep round dispatched to muse-spark-1.3-contributor (feat/cellref-sweep, laptop) covering ts typeof :135, ts member-call :1167, and php ~:4229 (verify-first; possibly no code needed there). Smoke-test duty on shiva post-sweep per the reciprocal note. Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\n2026-11-05 0x:xx +0700 — owner routing update: codex, agy, muse, qwen available; kimi CLI out (kimi via qwen allowed)\\\\nOwner: \\\\\\\"codex, agy, muse, qwen cli and their models are available. kimi cli is out, but you may use kimi from qwen cli.\\\\\\\" Measured: qwen probe OK (plan mode); implementation form is --approval-mode auto-edit, review form plan (reference lines 429-433). Board: implementation = muse-spark-1.3-contributor (proven) and qwen models (new capacity); architect = gpt-6.1-sol unchanged; agy = quota-walled until ~Nov 9-10; codex = available (sol primarily the architect per the earlier ruling; implementation-capable when the architect lane is idle). Also read: build-n-test.md boundary reconciliation (individual tests local; suite-scale remote only). Entered by the interactive ZCode seat (GLM-5.3-Flash).\\\\n---\\\\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\\\\n\\\\n## Domain Scope\\\\n\\\\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\\\\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\\\\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\\\\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\\\\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\\\\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\\\\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\\\\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\\\\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\\\\n\\\\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\\\\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\\\\n\\\\n## Core Responsibilities\\\\n\\\\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\\\\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\\\\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\\\\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\\\\n\\\\n## Delegation Prompt Template\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\\\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\\\n\\\\n# Task: <Task Name>\\\\n\\\\nRole: Lead System Architect\\\\n\\\\nImplementers:\\\\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\\\\n\\\\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\\\\n\\\\nRead first:\\\\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\\\\n- <target-design-file>\\\\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\\\\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\\\\n\\\\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\\\\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\\\\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\\\\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\\\\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\\\\n\\\\nBegin the final response exactly with:\\\\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\\\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\\\n\\\\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\\\\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_5\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n 'astra|Architect|Cost|codex|subscription' docs/agents/team.md; git status --short; git log -3 --oneline\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_5\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n 'astra|Architect|Cost|codex|subscription' docs/agents/team.md; git status --short; git log -3 --oneline\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"25:| [Architect](roles/architect.md)                   | Axioms, invariants, boundaries, architecture                                                           |\\\\n45:## Available Subscriptions & Cost Constraints\\\\n47:The Orchestrator routes work using these cost profiles. Flat subscriptions are preferred; metered models are reserved for tasks explicitly requiring them.\\\\n50:| Provider        | Cost Structure                         | Routing Notes                                                                                               |\\\\n52:| agy             | Flat: Included                         | Treated as a flat subscription. Use freely within budget.                                                   |\\\\n54:| qwen            | Token Plan subscription (Alibaba Cloud | The `qwen` CLI is Alibaba's own coding agent (`@qwen-code/qwen-code@0.17.0`, npm-global under nvm node      |\\\\n68:| codex           | Flat: ChatGPT Plus ($20/mo)            | Strict 