{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-aaq/BRIEF-aaq.md | head -130; nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-aaq/probe/aaq_probe.clj | head -140; nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-aaq/test/aaq_probe.clj | head -140; rg --files collab/yang-clojure | rg '(qwen|addendum)'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-05 04:00:00 GMT\n     2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-05 11:00:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n     3\tCoding-Agent: glm (glm-5.3) — the lane the owner chose for this unit's arc (r4/r5)\n     4\tSession-ID: not-applicable (orchestrator-dispatched, fresh session)\n     5\t# Task: implement the SIGNED attribution-as-query ruling — caller-side site tagging, derived site tables, the seven-case battery, the honest migration\n     6\t\n     7\tRole: compiler/harness engineer (glm). THE SPEC is the signed ruling-of-record: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling-of-record.md` — read it FIRST, implement exactly its rules R1-R7 and its implementation ordering. A fresh codex gate reviews against the ruling before landing. You have shell.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Context\n    10\t\n    11\tWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-aaq, branch attribution-as-query, base master 3eebe844e (the ruling landed; D2, cell/authentic?, H3-2, H3-3 all in). The governing reviews (astra/qwen/kimi) are linked from the ruling's header — kimi's v3 review found the mechanism flaw your implementation must respect: **site ids are CALLER-SIDE, at application expressions in the compiled AST, post-macroexpansion; the callee-entry record carries the CALLER's site id.** Callee-side tagging (v3's flaw) yields identical records for both origins and is forbidden.\n    12\t\n    13\t## The implementation, in the ruling's stated order\n    14\t\n    15\t1. **FIRST DELIVERABLE — the written inventory confirmation**: what the instrumentation change touches (kernel-trace-form's position, the walker's application-node stamping site, the callee-record extension), the capacity measurement (stream/make + the instruction bound vs the added trace field — R6), and the offset-table coverage list (every context-API arity kernel-context-extra-arguments served, latte_oracle_test.clj:1786). Write it BEFORE code; commit it as the round's first commit.\n    16\t2. **Caller-side site-id stamping**: application expressions in the compiled AST (post-macroexpansion — the corpus runs under is/testing/LaTTe macros; source-level tagging misses expanded sites) get compile-time-unique site ids; the callee-entry record becomes `[fname arity caller-site-id]`. The walker changes are AUTHORIZED by the ruling (R2) — scoped to application-node stamping + the record extension; nothing else in yin.vm moves.\n    17\t3. **Mechanically derived site tables**: the compiler derives each site's argument shape (ambient literal `empty-env` vs anything else) during instrumentation — the tables are DERIVED, not hand-declared (R7's trust model), recorded in a stable versioned evidence format (R1's condition b), with the canonical-source-hash per fixture (R2b case 3's referent).\n    18\t4. **The SEVEN-case battery + the stale-table diagnostic** (R2b): each case a real test; the three new ones (5 redefined as compile-time AST verification; 7 variable-argument default-refusal; 8 the stale-table diagnostic) written from the ruling's text.\n    19\t5. **The accounting rewrite + the honest pin migration** (R5/R6): kernel-executed-arity? to the 3-vector shape; the offset table retired with its coverage list stated; every 2-vector pin migrated — the mechanical updates AND the semantic /1 re-credit listed in the evidence per R5.\n    20\t6. **The attribution + re-credit**: F2's ambient-shape execution credits registered-definition?/1 through the ruled query; the evidence regenerates; the withdrawn-witness report if any.\n    21\t7. **H3-6 prep**: the attribution query's shape, stated for the audit (the audit itself is a separate round).\n    22\t\n    23\t## Verification (test-boundary ruling: focused local, suite-scale remote)\n    24\t\n    25\t- Local (individual): the seven-case battery, the migrated pins, the re-credit, kondo on every touched file. Real outputs.\n    26\t- REMOTE (list exact commands for the seat): the full oracle namespace (expect the by-design assertion to PASS FOR THE FIRST TIME — 165/165), yang.clojure-test, yang.base, the capacity restatement's confirmation.\n    27\t- If 165/165 does NOT hold on the remote run: STOP, report the withdrawn witnesses per R5 — do not force credit.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Boundaries\n    30\t\n    31\t- yin.vm: ONLY the application-node stamping + the callee-record extension (R2's authorization). No other VM changes. yang.clojure: untouched unless the stamping requires it (justify). The harness (latte_oracle_test.clj, context.edn, slice9_gate.md's versioned attribution section) is the main surface. The pin migrations are authorized by R5 — list every revised pin in the evidence.\n    32\t- Commit on the branch (inventory commit first); push (gh HTTPS if ssh unavailable); do NOT merge.\n    33\t\n    34\t## Report\n    35\t\n    36\tThe inventory (deliverable 1) in full; the diff per file; every local test's real output; the remote command list; any deviation from the ruling with its reason.\n     1\t(ns aaq-probe\n     2\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest]]\n     3\t            [clojure.pprint :as pp]))\n     4\t\n     5\t(defn probe []\n     6\t  (let [nsym 'yang.latte-oracle-test\n     7\t        ivars (ns-interns (find-ns nsym))\n     8\t        v (fn [s] (deref (get ivars s)))\n     9\t        corpus (v 'kernel-gate-corpus)\n    10\t        f2 (first (filter #(= :h3-2-elab-inferred-anonymous (:id %)) (:fixtures corpus)))\n    11\t        kc (v 'kernel-compile)\n    12\t        compiled (kc f2)]\n    13\t    (println \"status:\" (:status compiled))\n    14\t    (when (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n    15\t      (let [ast (:ast compiled)\n    16\t            sites (atom [])\n    17\t            walk-fn (fn walk [node path]\n    18\t                      (when (map? node)\n    19\t                        (when (= :application (:type node))\n    20\t                          (let [op (:operator node)]\n    21\t                            (when (and (= :variable (:type op))\n    22\t                                       (contains? '#{gate-defenv-registered-definition?\n    23\t                                                     registered-definition?}\n    24\t                                                (:name op)))\n    25\t                              (swap! sites conj {:path path\n    26\t                                                 :op (:name op)\n    27\t                                                 :operands (:operands node)}))))\n    28\t                        (doseq [[k v] node]\n    29\t                          (when (coll? v) (walk v (conj path k))))))\n    30\t            _ (walk-fn ast [])\n    31\t            simplify (fn simplify [n]\n    32\t                       (cond\n    33\t                         (map? n) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (simplify v)]) n))\n    34\t                         (vector? n) (mapv simplify n)\n    35\t                         (seq? n) (apply list (map simplify n))\n    36\t                         :else n))]\n    37\t        (println \"registered-definition? application sites:\" (count @sites))\n    38\t        (doseq [s @sites]\n    39\t          (pp/pprint (update s :operands simplify)))))))\n    40\t\n    41\t(deftest probe-test (probe))\n     1\t(ns aaq-probe\n     2\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest]]\n     3\t            [clojure.pprint :as pp]))\n     4\t\n     5\t(defn probe []\n     6\t  (require 'yang.latte-oracle-test)\n     7\t  (let [ivars (ns-interns (find-ns 'yang.latte-oracle-test))\n     8\t        v (fn [s] (deref (get ivars s)))\n     9\t        corpus (v 'kernel-gate-corpus)\n    10\t        f2 (first (filter #(= :h3-2-elab-inferred-anonymous (:id %)) (:fixtures corpus)))\n    11\t        call ((v 'kernel-c-program) f2)\n    12\t        forms ((v 'kernel-closure) call)]\n    13\t    (println \"FORM COUNT:\" (count forms))\n    14\t    (doseq [[i form] (map-indexed vector forms)]\n    15\t      (let [syms (set ((v 'walk-symbols) form))]\n    16\t        (when (or (contains? syms 'registered-definition?)\n    17\t                  (contains? syms 'gate-defenv-registered-definition?))\n    18\t          (println \"==== form\" i \"====\")\n    19\t          (pp/pprint form))))\n    20\t    (println \"==== the stub/kernel-source for registered-definition? ====\")\n    21\t    (pp/pprint (get (v 'kernel-sources) 'gate-defenv-registered-definition?))\n    22\t    (println \"==== initial-context ====\")\n    23\t    (pp/pprint (v 'initial-context))\n    24\t    nil))\n    25\t\n    26\t(deftest probe-test (probe))\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794610000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.qwen-review.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a.astra-review.stdout.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
