{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php.cljc | sed -n '640,696p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '2262,2342p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/repl.cljc | sed -n '80,114p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1867,1889p'; rg -n 'frontend-metadata|record|expan' src/cljc/yin/repl/ast_index.cljc | head -22\"","aggregated_output":"   640\t(defn compile-program\n   641\t  ([ast] (compile-program ast true))\n   642\t  ([ast tail?]\n   643\t   (let [stmts (:stmts ast)]\n   644\t     (if (empty? stmts)\n   645\t       (cond-> {:type :literal, :value nil} tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n   646\t       (let [head (first stmts)\n   647\t             rest-prog {:php-type :suite, :stmts (rest stmts)}]\n   648\t         (cond (= :function (:php-type head))\n   649\t               (cond-> {:type :application,\n   650\t                        :operator {:type :lambda,\n   651\t                                   :params [(:name head)],\n   652\t                                   :body (compile-program rest-prog tail?)},\n   653\t                        :operands [{:type :application,\n   654\t                                    :operator Z-combinator,\n   655\t                                    :operands [{:type :lambda,\n   656\t                                                :params [(:name head)],\n   657\t                                                :body {:type :lambda,\n   658\t                                                       :params (:params head),\n   659\t                                                       :body (compile-suite\n   660\t                                                               (:body head)\n   661\t                                                               true)}}]}]}\n   662\t                 tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n   663\t               (= :assignment (:php-type head))\n   664\t               (cond-> {:type :application,\n   665\t                        :operator {:type :lambda,\n   666\t                                   :params [(:name head)],\n   667\t                                   :body (compile-program rest-prog tail?)},\n   668\t                        :operands [(compile-stmt head false)]}\n   669\t                 tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n   670\t               (= 1 (count stmts)) (compile-stmt head tail?)\n   671\t               :else (cond-> {:type :application,\n   672\t                              :operator {:type :lambda,\n   673\t                                         :params ['_],\n   674\t                                         :body (compile-program rest-prog\n   675\t                                                                tail?)},\n   676\t                              :operands [(compile-stmt head false)]}\n   677\t                       tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))))\n   678\t\n   679\t\n   680\t(defn compile\n   681\t  [source]\n   682\t  (-> source\n   683\t      tokenize\n   684\t      parse-program\n   685\t      compile-program))\n  2262\t(defn lower-module-body\n  2263\t  \"The module's statements as one node, before the runtime wrapper: what\n  2264\t   lowering goldens compare.\"\n  2265\t  [packet]\n  2266\t  (module-body (context packet)))\n  2267\t\n  2268\t\n  2269\t(defn lower-unit\n  2270\t  \"One separately scoped module body as a function of its shared global\n  2271\t   receiver. Keeping this seam lets a host compose independently parsed\n  2272\t   units without concatenating source or reinitializing the runtime.\"\n  2273\t  [packet]\n  2274\t  (let [ctx (context packet)]\n  2275\t    (u/lam [(:this ctx)] (module-body ctx))))\n  2276\t\n  2277\t\n  2278\t(defn- with-runtime\n  2279\t  \"Both source entry points install the shared convention before JS.\"\n  2280\t  [prelude main]\n  2281\t  (u/mark-tails\n  2282\t    (case prelude\n  2283\t      :bundled (u/then prelude/uast main)\n  2284\t      :linked (u/seq-nodes [(app* 'require (u/lit 'yang.call))\n  2285\t                            (app* 'require (u/lit prelude/module-name))\n  2286\t                            (app* 'js/init!)\n  2287\t                            main]))))\n  2288\t\n  2289\t\n  2290\t(defn lower-units\n  2291\t  \"A complete program for multiple separately parsed units. The runtime is\n  2292\t   installed and initialized once; each unit receives its own lexical body\n  2293\t   while sharing the same global object and output stream.\"\n  2294\t  ([packets] (lower-units packets {}))\n  2295\t  ([packets {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n  2296\t   (let [units (mapv lower-unit packets)\n  2297\t         main (names/canonicalize\n  2298\t                (app* 'js/run-main\n  2299\t                      (u/lam ['this]\n  2300\t                             (if (seq units)\n  2301\t                               (u/seq-nodes\n  2302\t                                 (mapv (fn [unit] (u/app unit (u/v 'this))) units))\n  2303\t                               (u/lit :js/undefined)))))]\n  2304\t     (with-runtime prelude main))))\n  2305\t\n  2306\t\n  2307\t(defn lower-packet\n  2308\t  \"The complete program for one ok packet: the module body run by\n  2309\t   `js/run-main`, generated names canonicalized, tail calls marked. Its\n  2310\t   value is `{:js/out [...] :js/uncaught nil-or-snapshot}`.\n  2311\t\n  2312\t   `:prelude` selects how the runtime profile arrives: `:bundled` (the\n  2313\t   default) carries the prelude tree ahead of the body; `:linked` requires\n  2314\t   the modules `yang.call` and `js` from the task's link pair, then allocates\n  2315\t   the task's runtime state with `(js/init!)`.\"\n  2316\t  ([packet] (lower-packet packet {}))\n  2317\t  ([packet {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n  2318\t   (let [main (names/canonicalize (app* 'js/run-main (lower-unit packet)))]\n  2319\t     (with-runtime prelude main))))\n  2320\t\n  2321\t\n  2322\t(def program-medium\n  2323\t  \"The program medium's logical identity when the composition names none.\"\n  2324\t  :yang.ts/program)\n  2325\t\n  2326\t\n  2327\t(def ^:private stage-config\n  2328\t  {:diagnostic-ns diagnostic-ns,\n  2329\t   :program-medium program-medium,\n  2330\t   :ok? #(= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome %)),\n  2331\t   :lower (fn [state packet]\n  2332\t            (lower-packet packet {:prelude (get state :prelude :bundled)})),\n  2333\t   :option-keys [:prelude :dialect]})\n  2334\t\n  2335\t\n  2336\t(defn lower-transform\n  2337\t  \"The lowering stage's transform (`yang.core.stage/lower-transform`).\"\n  2338\t  [state packet]\n  2339\t  (core-stage/lower-transform stage-config state packet))\n  2340\t\n  2341\t\n  2342\t(defn open-stage\n    80\t               (str \"SyntaxError: \" (:message e)\n    81\t                    (when (:line e) (str \" (line \" (:line e) \")\"))))\n    82\t             {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/syntax\n    83\t              :errors (:yang.cst/errors packet)}))))\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\t(defn lower-session\n    87\t  \"`[ast session']` for one ok CST `packet` under `session` (nil on a fresh\n    88\t   session, `:primed` once the prelude has run).\"\n    89\t  [packet session]\n    90\t  (let [packet (ok-packet! packet)\n    91\t        packet (cond-> packet\n    92\t                 (not (contains? packet :yang.python.antlr/max-digits))\n    93\t                 (assoc :yang.python.antlr/max-digits 4300))\n    94\t        _ (p/validate! packet {:diagnostic-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"})\n    95\t        body (lower/lower-module-body packet nil true)\n    96\t        main (u/let1 '%repl-body\n    97\t                     (u/lam [lower/globals-sym lower/globals-fn-sym] body)\n    98\t                     (u/sexp->uast run-form))\n    99\t        ast (u/mark-tails (if (= :primed session)\n   100\t                            main\n   101\t                            (u/then prelude/uast main)))]\n   102\t    [ast :primed]))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(defn lower\n   106\t  \"The stateless lowering: a program that carries the prelude.\"\n   107\t  [packet]\n   108\t  (first (lower-session packet nil)))\n  1867\t  is the identity it then fetches. A record leading from a different\n  1868\t  tree, or to a different identity, is `:derivation-mismatch`. Four\n  1869\t  individually valid images from four different trees therefore cannot\n  1870\t  share a manifest, and a swapped image fails before load.\n  1871\t- **Three contracts, kept apart.** A manifest carries a schema version\n  1872\t  and a per-format contract map, and neither is the other:\n  1873\t  - `:yin.module/schema` versions the manifest container itself: which\n  1874\t    keys exist and what they mean. It is checked by the\n  1875\t    `:yin.module/manifest` format record's validator, which implements\n  1876\t    exactly one schema version; a manifest of another version is\n  1877\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`. It says nothing about any\n  1878\t    bytecode.\n  1879\t  - `:yin.module/contracts` maps each format the manifest lowered to\n  1880\t    the execution contract that format's image targets: the UCF stamp\n  1881\t    `\"v3\"` for the semantic vector and the tree, the stack lowering\n  1882\t    contract `\"b2\"` for the stack image, the register contract `\"r2\"`\n  1883\t    for the register image. These are the Rule R revisions; a manifest\n  1884\t    naming \"v2\", \"b1\", or \"r1\" is `:contract-mismatch`, with no\n  1885\t    migration. A format present under `:yin.module/derivations`\n  1886\t    must be present here; one that is not is `:descriptor-defect` with\n  1887\t    rule `:contract-missing`.\n  1888\t  - A format record's `:contract` (section 4.1) is the one execution\n  1889\t    contract that record implements, and a request's\n3:   occurrence relation over every program the session expanded\n24:   one already held at its address, or a failed derivation is recorded\n108:  \"Merge one packet's rows and occurrences, or record why it could not be\n188:   expanded programs, never on which evaluator ran them, so every VM\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
